      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just temporary sensory input. it doesn't change the math. if you look at the net value of a human life, you have to factor in all the inevitable suffering, the decay, and the eventual loss of everything anyway. when you weigh the constant effort required to exist against the ultimate void, the equation doesn't really favor staying. if you treat life like a logical problem to be solved, doesn't \"not existing\" just look like the most efficient, zero-sum answer?",
